§3 CONVENTIONS NAMED BEFORE SCORING
====================================================================================================
  E(ns) = I − R·Z²/(n − δ)²  with I = 892,700 (L6914, ±400 not applied to the point values: L7018–L7019 "to be added at both edges"),
  Z = 6 (L7075: Z_eff = 6 — the Rydberg electron outside Sc⁵⁺), R = R∞ = 109737.31568160 cm⁻¹ (CODATA 2018; L9183 "R* is the only import")
  rival R_Sc = R∞/(1 + m_e/M(⁴⁵Sc)) = 109735.97662 (reduced mass, A = 44.955908) — tested as convention R2
  δ(4s) = 1.0057, δ(5s) = 0.9812 READ from L7004 (inputs, not computed; C.3 L10287 "the input defects … not recomputed")
  Ritz two-point: δ₂ = (δ₄ − δ₅)/(1/16 − 1/25), δ∞ = δ₄ − δ₂/16, δ(ns) = δ∞ + δ₂/n²; convex tangent δ(6s) ≥ 2δ(5s) − δ(4s); 7s tangent 2δ(6s) − δ(5s)
  chain convention U: every δ carried unrounded (prec 40); chain convention P: each δ quantized to the 4 dp the book prints before use
  Rule 4 constant defect δ̄ = (δ₄ + δ₅)/2 (L6114 "the constant form"); printed 0.9934 — 0.99345 at ROUND_HALF_EVEN → 0.9934, at half-up → 0.9935: the book's 4 dp is the half-even (or truncated) form
  λ = 10⁷/E nm; eV = E·hc/e with hc/e = 1.239841984e-4 eV·cm; all figures quantized ROUND_HALF_EVEN at the printed precision

